{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"First plan review BLOCKed with one blocking finding (E4) and two advisories. All three were correct.\n\nThe blocking finding: the census omitted `tests/unit/workflow/test_review_skeleton.py` (lines 104, 117), so AC7's promised four-path residue was wrong. Root cause is a sequencing error on my part, not a miscount — slice 9 (`9b96-18b7-b19e-4f85`) repoints that file onto `spec-alignment`, and I took the census on slice 9's tree while plan review pins material at `origin/main`, which does not yet carry slice 9. The reviewer was reading the real tree and I was reading a future one.\n\nFix: added an explicit Ordering section naming slice 9 as a hard predecessor and stating what a tree-wide grep reports until it lands. The census itself is unchanged and correct for the post-slice-9 tree.\n\nAdvisory 1 (COH/E1): the summary said \"no documentation changes\" while AC4/AC6 require a `docs/release-notes.md` addition. Summary reworded to carve the release-note entry out explicitly, and the out-of-scope paragraph now explains that release-notes' *existing* `ticket-quality` mentions are left alone because the file is historical narrative.\n\nAdvisory 2 (P6, DET, minor): the ACs used a `$F7` shell variable inside the grep and pytest commands, which expands before the command runs, so the written pattern is not what executes. Every AC now spells the seven paths out literally, and AC3 describes the collect-and-sort pipeline in prose rather than embedding `grep '::'`.\n\nRe-review is deliberately deferred until slice 9 is on `origin/main`; re-running it before then would reproduce the same blocking finding against the same unchanged tree."},"env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1793309260921434730,"uuid":"fbc9451d-a400-435f-8850-c8a5cc3c8904"}